@@ -0,0 +1,141 @@
+Reviewer-authored exhaustive local inventory
+=============================================
+
+Files in scope
+--------------
+semantic.k, verification.k, and the reachability claim in spec.k. There are no
+generated helper K source files. Built candidate *-kompiled trees were excluded.
+
+Local syntax and configuration
+------------------------------
+MPY-SYNTAX:
+1. Program ::= Module(Stmts)
+2. Stmts ::= List{Stmt, ""} (zero or more statements, concatenated)
+3. Stmt ::= FuncDef(String, Params, Stmts)
+4. Stmt ::= Assign(Expr, Expr)
+5. Stmt ::= If(Expr, Stmts, Stmts)
+6. Stmt ::= Return(Expr)
+7. Params ::= Params(Strings)
+8. Strings ::= List{String, ","}
+9. Expr ::= Name(String)
+10. Expr ::= Int(Int)
+11. Expr ::= ListExpr(Exprs)
+12. Expr ::= Compare(Expr, CmpOps)
+13. Expr ::= BinOp(String, Expr, Expr)
+14. Exprs ::= List{Expr, ","}
+15. CmpOps ::= List{CmpOp, ","}
+16. CmpOp ::= CmpOp(String, Expr)
+
+MPY:
+17. Input ::= pair(Int, Int)
+18. Value ::= intVal(Int)
+19. Value ::= boolVal(Bool)
+20. Value ::= listVal(List)
+21. Result ::= noResult
+22. Result ::= Value
+23. KItem ::= exec(Stmts)
+24. KItem ::= execStmt(Stmt)
+25. KItem ::= eval(Expr)
+26. KItem ::= assignTo(String)
+27. KItem ::= binRight(String, Value)
+28. KItem ::= cmpLeft(String, Expr)
+29. KItem ::= cmpRight(String, Value)
+30. KItem ::= choose(Stmts, Stmts)
+31. KItem ::= returnValue
+32. Value ::= evalPlaceholder(Expr), an internal scheduling marker
+33. Configuration <py> contains <k>:Program, <input>:pair(Int,Int),
+    <env>:.Map, and <result>:noResult.
+
+VERIFICATION:
+34. List ::= expectedDigit(Int,Int,Int) [function]
+35. List ::= expected(Int,Int) [function]
+
+There are no local total, functional, simplification, concrete, opaque,
+priority, macro, or anywhere declarations. The only local attributes are the
+two [function] attributes above.
+
+Operational rules in semantic.k
+-------------------------------
+S1 (59-62): exact entry harness for Module(FuncDef("generate_integers",
+Params("a","b"),BODY)); loads A and B into the initially empty environment and
+executes BODY. It does not calculate or assume the answer.
+
+S2 (64): an empty statement sequence finishes.
+S3 (65): a nonempty statement sequence executes its head then its tail.
+
+S4 (67): assignment to Name(X) evaluates the RHS before assignment.
+S5 (68-69): a completed Value updates X in <env> and consumes assignTo.
+
+S6 (71-72): If evaluates its condition before selecting a branch.
+S7 (73): boolVal(true) selects THEN.
+S8 (74): boolVal(false) selects ELSE.
+
+S9 (76): Return evaluates its expression then schedules returnValue.
+S10 (77-78): returnValue writes the resulting Value to <result>.
+
+S11 (80): integer literal evaluation yields intVal(I).
+S12 (81-82): Name(X) reads the matching value from <env>.
+S13 (83): an empty list expression yields listVal(.List).
+S14 (84): a singleton integer list yields listVal(ListItem(I)).
+
+S15 (86-87): BinOp schedules LEFT before RIGHT, storing RIGHT in the internal
+evalPlaceholder marker.
+S16 (90-91): after LEFT is a Value, evaluate RIGHT and retain LEFT.
+S17 (92-93): list "+" concatenates the retained left K List before the right
+K List, matching Python list concatenation for the used values.
+
+S18 (95-96): Compare schedules LEFT before RIGHT.
+S19 (97-98): after LEFT is a Value, evaluate RIGHT and retain LEFT.
+S20 (99-101): "<=" yields true exactly when LEFT <=Int RIGHT.
+S21 (102-104): "<=" yields false under the Boolean complement.
+
+Proof-local function equations in verification.k
+-------------------------------------------------
+V1 (9-11): expectedDigit(A,B,D) is ListItem(D) when D lies in either ordered
+orientation of the inclusive interval.
+V2 (12-15): expectedDigit(A,B,D) is .List under the exact Boolean complement.
+V3 (17-21): expected(A,B) concatenates expectedDigit for 2,4,6,8 in ascending
+order.
+
+Rule decisions and scope
+------------------------
+S1 is a purpose-specific invocation harness, not general Python module/call
+semantics. For the exact submitted single-function Module, it binds the two
+arguments correctly and executes the submitted body. S2-S8 and S11-S21 are
+ordinary deterministic small-step rules that agree with the target operations
+on every reachable target state. The two comparison guards are disjoint and
+exhaustive. The list-add rule has the correct left/right order.
+
+S9-S10 agree with the target because its sole Return is the final statement.
+They are not a reusable implementation of abrupt Python return: in a different
+program with statements after Return, S3 would preserve and execute that
+suffix. This is a documented out-of-scope generality limitation, not a false
+conclusion enabled by the submitted program for any positive input.
+
+evalPlaceholder is an internal scheduling constructor declared in Value so it
+can occupy binRight's Value field. No source Expr production can construct it,
+and no reachable target path returns, assigns, compares, or branches on it.
+
+V1 and V2 are mathematically true, disjoint, and exhaustive because their
+guards are P and notBool(P). V3 is an unconditional truthful definition.
+Neither expected function replaces program execution; both occur only in the
+destination pattern. There are no operational bridges, opaque values, helper
+claims, loop claims, or oracle rules.
+
+Used-construct coverage map
+---------------------------
+Module/FuncDef/Params -> syntax 1,3,7,8; S1
+statement sequence -> syntax 2; S2-S3
+Assign/Name -> syntax 4,9; S4-S5,S12
+If -> syntax 5; S6-S8
+Return -> syntax 6; S9-S10 (final-position target use)
+Int -> syntax 10; S11
+empty/singleton ListExpr -> syntax 11,14; S13-S14
+BinOp("+") -> syntax 13; S15-S17
+Compare/CmpOp("<=") -> syntax 12,15,16; S18-S21
+environment state -> configuration 33; S1,S5,S12
+result state -> configuration 33; S10
+
+No target construct relies on a missing rule. No heap, allocation identity,
+exceptions, calls within the body, loops, output, mutation through aliasing, or
+other state components occur in solution.mpy.
